    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on maximizing efficiency against mid-tier arms, headlined by **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who checks in with our highest score of 76.21. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a 14% platoon advantage against Kyle Bradish, making him a locked-in must-start. **Jose Caballero** (74.61) and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) follow closely as high-leverage plays. **Jose Caballero** takes advantage of a soft matchup against PJ Poulin (xERA 5.53), while **Seiya Suzuki** leverages a strong BvP history (25 PA) and a favorable platoon spot against Nick Lodolo to bolster his floor.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Naylor**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 53.42. Despite solid underlying metrics, **Josh Naylor** faced negative park and SP skill adjustments that ultimately pushed him behind the production threshold of starters like **Isaac Paredes** (66.69). We are keeping a close eye on **Brice Turang** on the bench; while his potential for stolen bases is tempting, he is currently benched due to a sub-50 score, a tough matchup against Graham Ashcraft, and a 32% rain risk that renders his start volatile.\n\nManagerial caution is advised regarding **James Wood** and **Corbin Carroll**. **James Wood** boasts an elite .432 xwOBA, but his 53.19 score is hampered by a significant SP skill penalty against a high-tier arm in Cam Schlittler. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** faces the difficult Yoshinobu Yamamoto; while his elite speed makes him a roster staple, the 15% SP skill penalty and Yamamoto\u2019s ability to hold runners (58% SB limitation) suppress his daily efficiency to 59.02. We will monitor all \"Lineup Pending\" designations closely, particularly for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**, to ensure the projected batting order holds before first pitch.",
